    bestPractices: ["Users can access the core capability through a responsive frontend.","UI state, server state and navigation state have explicit ownership.","Async operations expose loading, success, empty and failure states.","The system supports recovery from expected failures."],
    tradeOffs: "| Decision | Benefit | Cost / Risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| SSR | Fast content delivery/SEO | Server complexity |\n| CSR | Simple client model | Initial UX/SEO trade-offs |\n| Micro frontend | Team independence | Runtime/build complexity |\n| Monolith | Simpler operations | Larger coordination boundary |\n| Global state | Shared access | Coupling/re-render risk |\n| Local state | Encapsulation | Duplication if shared incorrectly |\n| CDN caching | Lower latency/origin load | Invalidation complexity |",
